                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "215516532",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198330888468",
                            "num_reviews": 820,
                            "playtime_forever": 199,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 199,
                            "last_played": 1767927449
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It was okay, took some getting used to, but in the end I had fun. \nYou do have to go into the menu A LOT. You can equip some items, but it doesn't seem to tell you when they break, so you want to check a lot to see if you need to put on a new on.\nAlso when you get to the edge of the map, you need to hit enter or space to go through, most of the time, the game didn't tell me this, Frustrating until I figured it out. \nYou also want to save a lot, especially in the early goings. I would suggest after ever combat and encounter. \nThe game itself is pretty much a series of fetch quests, a ton of wandering monsters, but with a compelling enough through story. \nThere was one item that seems to hint at maybe there will be more? Not sure... \nAll in all, a single thumb up, not a great game, but it took me three hours to beat, including a half a dozen failed attempts. Not too shabby. Pretty sure I got it on sale though...",
